    {
      "id": "hadith_000333",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 333",
      "hadith_number": "333",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن ابن عمر رضي الله عنهما قال: كانت تحتي امرأة، وكنت أحبها، وكان عمر يكرهها، فقال لي: طلقها، فأبيت، فأتى عمر رضي الله عنه النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، فذكر ذلك له، فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: \"طلقها\".",
      "text_tr": "Berâ b. Âzib’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Hz. Peygamber şöyle buyurmuştur: Teyze, anne gibidir.",
      "text_en": "Ibn 'Umar (May Allah be pleased with them) reported: I had a wife whom I loved but 'Umar (May Allah be pleased with him) disliked her. He asked me to divorce her and when I refused, 'Umar (May Allah be pleased with him) went to Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and mentioned the matter to him. Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked me to divorce her.",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/333:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/333:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/333:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001035",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1035",
      "hadith_number": "1035",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي مالك الأشعري رضي الله عنه قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم \"الطهور شطر الإيمان\" وقد سبق بطوله في باب الصبر. وفي الباب حديث عمرو بن عبسة رضي الله عنه السابق في آخر باب الرجاء، وهو حديث عظيم، مشتمل على جمل من الخيرات.",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Mâlik el-Eş’arî’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah : Temizlik, imanın yarısıdır, demiştir.",
      "text_en": "Abu Malik Al-Ash'ari (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Purification is half the Iman.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1035:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1035:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1035:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001178",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1178",
      "hadith_number": "1178",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن ابن مسعود رضي الله عنه، قال: صليت مع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ، ليلة، فلم يزل قائمًا حتى هممت بأمر سوء. قيل: ما هممت؟ قال: هممت أن أجلس وأدعه.",
      "text_tr": "Âişe’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Hz. Peygamber gecenin başında uyur, sonunda ise kalkıp namaz kılardı.",
      "text_en": "Ibn Mas'ud (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: One night I joined the Prophet (ﷺ) in his (optional) Salat. He (ﷺ) prolonged the Qiyam (standing) so much that I made up my mind to commit an act of wrong. He was questioned: \"What did you intend to do?\" He replied: \"I intended to sit down and stop following him (in Salat).\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1178:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1178:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1178:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001658",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1658",
      "hadith_number": "1658",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي موسى الأشعري رضي الله عنه قال: احترق بيت بالمدينة على أهله من الليل، فلما حدث رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم بشأنهم قال: \"إن هذه النار عدو لكم، فإذا نمتم فأطفئوها\"",
      "text_tr": "Câbir’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah , kişinin nalınını/ayakkabısını ayakta giymesini yasakladı.",
      "text_en": "Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari (May Allah be pleased with him) said: A house in Al-Madinah was burnt with its occupants inside it one night. When this was reported to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said, \"Fire is your enemy. So, put it out before going to bed.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1658:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1658:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1658:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001207",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1207",
      "hadith_number": "1207",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي هريرة رضي الله عنه، عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: \"الفطرة خمس، أو خمس من الفطرة: الختان، والاستحداد، وتقليم الأظفار، ونتف الإبط، وقص الشارب\" (24)",
      "text_tr": "Âişe’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Hz. Peygamber : Misvak, ağzı temizler, Rabbi de hoşnut eder, buyurmuştur.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \"There are five acts which conform to the pure nature: Circumcision, removing of the pubic hair, clipping the nails, plucking the underarm hair and trimming the moustache.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1207:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1207:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1207:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001820",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1820",
      "hadith_number": "1820",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي سعيد الخدري رضي الله عنه عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: “يخرج الدجال فيتوجه قبله رجل من المؤمنين فيتلقاه المسالح: مسالح الدجال، فيقولون له: إلى أين تعمد؟ فيقول: أعمد إلى هذا الذي خرج فيقولون له أوَ ما تؤمن بربنا؟ فيقول: ما بربنا خفاء! فيقولون: اقتلوه، فيقول بعضهم لبعض: أليس قد نهاكم ربكم أن تقتلوا أحداً دونه، فينطلقون به إلى الدجال، فإذا رآه المؤمن قال: يا أيها الناس إن هذا الدجال الذي ذكر رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم ؛ فيأمر الدجال به فيشبّح؛ فيقول: خذوه وشجوه، فيوسع ظهره وبطنه ضرباً، فيقول: أوَ ما تؤمن بي؟ فيقول: أنت المسيح الكذاب! فيؤمر به ، فيؤشر بالمنشار من مفرقه حتى يفرق بين رجليه، ثم يمشي الدجال بين القطعتين ، ثم يقول له: قم ، فيستوي قائماً، ثم يقول له: أتؤمن بي؟ فيقول: ما ازددت فيك إلا بصيرة، ثم يقول: يا أيها الناس إنه لا يفعل بعدي بأحد من الناس، فيأخذه الدجال ليذبحه، فيجعل الله ما بين رقبته إلى ترقوته نحاساً، فلا يستطيع إليه سبيلا، فيأخذ بيديه ورجليه فيقذف به، فيحسب الناس أنما قذفه إلى النار، وإنما ألقي في الجنة\" فقال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم : \"هذا أعظم الناس شهادة عند رب العالمين\" وروى البخاري بعضه بمعناه “المسالح” :هم الخفراء والطلائع.",
      "text_tr": "Ümmü Şerîk (ra), Resûlullah’tan şöyle işittiğini nakletmiştir: İnsanlar, Deccal(in şerrin)den dağlara kaçacaklar.",
      "text_en": "Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, \"Dajjal (the Antichrist) will come forth and a person from amongst the believers will go towards him and the armed watchmen of Dajjal will meet him and they will say to him: 'Where do you intend to go?' He will say: 'I intend to go to this one who has appeared.' They will say to him: 'Don't you believe in our lord (meaning Dajjal)?' He will say: 'There (i.e., we know Him to be Allah, Alone, without any partners) is nothing hidden about our Rubb.' Some of them will say: 'Let us kill him', but some others will say: 'Has your lord (Dajjal) not forbidden you to kill anyone without his consent?' So they will take him to Dajjal. When the believer will see him, he will say: 'O people! This is Dajjal about whom the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has informed us.' Dajjal will have him laid on his stomach and have his head. He will be struck on his back and on his stomach. Dajjal will ask him: 'Don't you believe in me?' He will say: 'You are the false Messiah.' He will then give his order to have him sawn with a saw into two from the parting of his hair up to his legs. After that Dajjal will walk between the two halves and will say to him: 'Stand up', and he will stand on his feet. He will then say to him: 'Don't you believe in me?' The person will say: 'It has added to my insight that you are Dajjal'. He will add: 'O people! He will not be able to behave with anyone amongst people in such a manner after me.' Dajjal will try to kill him. The space between his neck and collarbone will turn into copper and he will find no way to kill him. So he will catch hold of him by his hand and feet and throw him into (what appears to be the fire). The people will think that he has been thrown into the fire whereas he will be thrown into Jannah.\" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) added, \"He will be the most eminent amongst the people with regard to martyrdom near the Rubb of the worlds.\"",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1820:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1820:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1820:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001794",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1794",
      "hadith_number": "1794",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي بكر رضي الله عنه أن رجلا ذُكر عند النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ، فأثنى عليه رجل خيرًا، فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم : \"ويحك! قطعت عنق صاحبك\" يقوله مرارًا \"وإن كان أحدكم مادحًا لا محالة، فليقل: أحسب كذا وكذا إن كان يرى أنه كذلك وحسيبه الله، ولا يزكي على الله أحدًا\"",
      "text_tr": "Enes’ten (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre o, şöyle demiştir: Peygamberimiz , (kendisine sunulan) güzel kokuyu reddetmezdi.",
      "text_en": "Abu Bakrah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: Mention of a man was made to the Prophet (ﷺ) and someone praised him whereupon he (ﷺ) said, \"Woe be to you! You have broken the neck of your friend!\" He repeated this several times and added, \"If one of you has to praise his friend at all, he should say: 'I reckon him to be such and such and Allah knows him well', if you think him to be so-and-so, you will be accountable to Allah because no one can testify the purity of others against Allah.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1794:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1794:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1794:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001288",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1288",
      "hadith_number": "1288",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أنس رضي الله عنه، أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم حج على رحل وكانت زاملته.",
      "text_tr": "Enes’ten (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah deve üzerinde hacca gitti. Erzak ve eşyası da aynı deve üzerinde idi.",
      "text_en": "Anas (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the pilgrimage on an unsaddled camel which also carried his provisions (i.e., his Zamilah).",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1288:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1288:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1288:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000595",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 595",
      "hadith_number": "595",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن عطية بن عروة السعدى الصحابي رضي الله عنه قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: \"لا يبلغ العبد أن يكون من المتقين حتى يدع مالا بأس به حذرا لما به بأس\".",
      "text_tr": "Hasan b. Ali şöyle demiştir: Ben Peygamber’in şu sözünü hafızamda tuttum: “Sana şüphe veren şeyi bırak, şüphe vermeyene bak.”",
      "text_en": "'Atiyyah bin 'Urwah As-Sa'di (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"No one will attain complete righteousness until he abandons (certain) unobjectionable (but doubtful) things so as to remain on his guard against something objectionable.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/595:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/595:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/595:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000968",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 968",
      "hadith_number": "968",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "عن أنس، رضي الله عنه، قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم : \"عليكم بالدلجة، فإن الأرض تطوي بالليل\" الدلجة : السير في الليل",
      "text_tr": "Enes’ten (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlulah : Gece yol almaya bakın, zira geceleyin daha hızlı mesafe kat edilir, buyurdu.",
      "text_en": "Anas (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"Keep to travelling by night because the earth is folded (traversed more easily) during the night.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/968:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/968:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/968:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000729",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 729",
      "hadith_number": "729",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي هريرة رضي الله عنه أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: “ إذا لبستم،وإذا توضأتم، فابدؤا بأيمانكم” حديث صحيح،",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah : Giyinirken ve abdest alırken sağ tarafınızdan başlayın, buyurmuştur.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"When you wear your clothes or perform your Wudu', begin with your right side.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/729:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/729:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/729:en",
