    {
      "id": "hadith_001279",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1279",
      "hadith_number": "1279",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعنه قال سمعت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول: \"من حج، فلم يرفث ولم يفسق، رجع كيوم ولدته أمه\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’nin (ra) işittiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle demiştir: Kötü söz söylemeden ve günah işlemeden hacceden kimse, annesinden doğduğu günkü (gibi günahsız) hâle döner.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"Whoever performs Hajj (pilgrimage) and does not have sexual relations (with his wife), nor commits sin, nor disputes unjustly (during Hajj), then he returns from Hajj as pure and free from sins as on the day on which his mother gave birth to him.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1279:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1279:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1279:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001292",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1292",
      "hadith_number": "1292",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي ذر رضي الله عنه قال: قلت يا رسول الله أي العمل أفضل؟ قال: \"الإيمان بالله والجهاد في سبيله\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Zer’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre o, şöyle demiştir: –Yâ Resûlallah, hangi amel daha faziletlidir, dedim. –Allah’a iman etmek ve O’nun yolunda cihad etmek, buyurdu.",
      "text_en": "Abu Dharr (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked: \"Which deed is the best?\" He (ﷺ) replied, \"Faith in Allah and Jihad (fighting, struggle) in the Cause of Allah.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1292:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1292:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1292:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001782",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1782",
      "hadith_number": "1782",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن ابن عباس رضي الله عنهما قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم : “لا تتلقوا الركبان، ولا يبع حاضر لباد\" فقال له طاوس: ما قوله: لا بيع حاضر لباد؟ قال: لا يكون له سمسارًا.",
      "text_tr": "Enes’ten (ra) rivayet edildiği üzere şöyle demiştir: Resûlullah , şehirlinin –ana baba bir kardeş dahi olsa– simsarlık ederek köylünün malını (ücretle) satmasını yasakladı.",
      "text_en": "Ibn 'Abbas (May Allah be pleased with them) said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"The caravans carrying merchandise should not be met on the way to purchase from them; a man in the city should not sell for a man of the desert.\"Tawus asked him (Ibn 'Abbas): \"What do these words really imply?\" He said: \"He should not work as an agent on his behalf.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1782:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1782:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1782:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000308",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 308",
      "hadith_number": "308",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعنه أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: \" من كان يؤمن بالله واليوم الآخر، فلا يؤذِ جاره، ومن كان يؤمن بالله واليوم الآخر، فليكرم ضيفه، ومن كان يؤمن بالله واليوم الآخر، فليقل خيرًا أو ليسكت\"",
      "text_tr": "Hz. Âişe (ra) anlatıyor: –Yâ Resûlallah , iki komşum var, ikramda bulunurken hangisinden başlayayım, diye sordum. Resûlullah : –Sana kapısı en yakın olan komşunla, buyurdu.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"He who believes in Allah and the Last Day let him not harm his neighbour; and he who believes in Allah and the Last Day let him show hospitality to his guest; and he who believes in Allah and the Last Day let him speak good or remain silent\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/308:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/308:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/308:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001280",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1280",
      "hadith_number": "1280",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعنه أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: \"العمرة إلى العمرة كفارة لما بينهما، والحج المبرور ليس له جزاء إلا الجنة\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah : İki umre, aralarında işlenen günahlara kefârettir; kabul olunmuş bir haccın mükâfatı ise ancak cennettir, buyurdu.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"(The performance of) 'Umrah is an expiation for the sins committed between it and the previous 'Umrah; and the reward of Hajj Mabrur (i.e., one accepted) is nothing but Jannah.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1280:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1280:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1280:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000400",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 400",
      "hadith_number": "400",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن ابن عمر رضي الله عنهما أن رسول الله، صلى الله عليه وسلم، قال \" يقوم الناس لرب العالمين حتى يغيب أحدهم في رشحه إلى أنصاف أذنيه\" ((و الرشح : العرق)).",
      "text_tr": "İbn Mes’ûd’dan (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle buyurmuştur: O gün cehennem, her birini yetmiş bin meleğin çektiği yetmiş bin yularla (bağlı olarak) getirilir.",
      "text_en": "Ibn 'Umar (May Allah be pleased with them) reported: I heard Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as saying, \"Mankind will stand before Allah, the Rubb of the worlds (on the Day of Resurrection), some of them will stand submerged in perspiration up to half of their ears\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/400:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/400:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/400:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001344",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1344",
      "hadith_number": "1344",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي سعيد رضي الله عنه قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم : \"ما من عبد يصوم يومًا في سبيل الله إلا باعد الله بذلك اليوم وجهه عن النار سبعين خريفًا\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Saîd’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle demiştir: Allah yolunda bir gün oruç tutan kimsenin yüzünü Allah, cehennemden yetmiş senelik mesafe uzaklaştırır.",
      "text_en": "Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"Every slave of Allah who observes Saum (fasting) for a day in the Cause of Allah, Allah will keep his face from Hell-fire at a distance of seventy years.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1344:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1344:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1344:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000238",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 238",
      "hadith_number": "238",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي هريرة رضي الله عنه أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: \"حق المسلم على المسلم خمس: رد السلام، وعيادة المريض، واتباع الجنائز وإجابة الدعوة، وتشميت العاطس\" و في رواية لمسلم: \"حق المسلم على المسلم ست: اذا لقيته فسلم عليه، و اذا دعاك فأجبه، و اذا استنصحك فانصح له، و اذا عطس فحمد الله فشمته، و اذا مرض فعده، و اذا مات فاتبعه.\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Peygamber şöyle buyurmuştur: Bir insan, dünyada diğer bir insanın ayıbını örterse, Allah da kıyamet gününde onun ayıbını örter.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah bepleased with him) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"A believer owes another believer five rights: responding to greetings, visiting him in illness, following his funeral, accepting his invitation, and saying 'Yarhamuk-Allah (May Allah have mercy on you),' when he says 'Al-hamdu lillah (Praise be to Allah)' after sneezing\".Muslim's narration is, \"There are six rights of a Muslim upon a Muslim: When you meet him, greet him; when he invites you, respond to him; when he seeks counsel, give him advice; when he sneezes and praises Allah, say to him: 'May Allah have mercy on you (Yarhamuk-Allah)'; when he is sick, visit him; and when he dies, follow his funeral\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/238:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/238:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/238:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000669",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 669",
      "hadith_number": "669",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن عبد الله بن مسعود رضي الله عنه قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم : “إنها ستكون بعدى أثرة، وأمور تنكرونها!” قالوا: يا رسول الله، كيف تأمر من أدرك منا ذلك؟ قال: “تؤدون الحق الذى عليكم، وتسألون الله الذى لكم”",
      "text_tr": "Enes’ten (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle buyurmuştur: Başı siyah üzüm gibi olan Habeşli bir köle dahi başınıza yönetici yapılsa onu dinleyin ve ona itaat edin.",
      "text_en": "'Abdullah bin Mas'ud (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"There will be discrimination after my death and there will be other matters that you will disapprove.\" He was asked: \"O Messenger of Allah! What do you command us to do when we are encountered with such happenings?\" He answered, \"Give what is due from you and supplicate to Allah for your rights.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/669:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/669:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/669:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001783",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1783",
      "hadith_number": "1783",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي هريرة رضي الله عنه قال: نهى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم أن يبيع حاضر لباد، ولا تناجشوا ولا يبيع الرجل على بيع أخيه، ولا يخطب على خطبة أخيه، ولا تسأل المرأة طلاق أختها لتكفأ ما في إنائها. وفي رواية قال: نهى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم عن التلقي وأن يبتاع المهاجر للأعرابي، وأن تشترط المرأة طلاق أختها، وأن يستام الرجل على سوم أخيه، ونهى عن النجش والتصرية\"",
      "text_tr": "İbn Ömer’den nakledildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle buyurmuştur: (Köylünün) satılık malını, (pazar yerine getirip piyasayı öğreninceye kadar) yolda karşıla(yıp satın al)mayın.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade that a man in the city should be the commission agent of a man from the desert and prohibited the practice of Najsh (i.e., offering a high price for something in order to allure another customer who is interested in the thing); and that a man should make an offer while the offer of his brother is pending; or that he should make a proposal of marriage while that of his brother is pending; or that a woman should try that a sister of hers might be divorced so that she might take her place.Another narration is: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade the people from meeting the caravan on the way for entering into business transaction with them; and the selling of the goods by a dweller of the city on behalf of a man of the desert; and the seeking by a woman the divorce of her sister (from her husband); and the practice of Najsh and leaving the animals unmilked (for sometime for the purpose of accumulation of milk to deceive the buyer).",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1783:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1783:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1783:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001310",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1310",
      "hadith_number": "1310",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن ابن عباس، رضي الله عنهما قال: سمعت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول: “عينان لا تمسهما النار عين بكت من خشية الله، وعين باتت تحرس في سبيل الله\"",
      "text_tr": "İbn Abbâs’ın (ra) işittiğine göre Allah Resûlü : Şu iki göze cehennem ateşi dokunmaz: Allah korkusundan ağlayan göz ve Allah rızası için gece nöbet bekleyen göz, buyurmuştur.",
      "text_en": "Ibn 'Abbas (May Allah be pleased with them) reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, \"Two eyes will never be touched by the fire of Hell; an eye which weeps out of Fear of Allah and an eye which spends the night in guarding in the Cause of Allah .\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1310:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1310:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1310:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000101",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 101",
      "hadith_number": "101",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "السابع: عنه أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: \" حجبت النار بالشهوات، وحجبت الجنة بالمكاره\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Peygamber şöyle buyurmuştur: Cehennem, nefsin arzu ettiği şehevî şeylerle, cennet ise nefsin hoşlanmadığı şeylerle perdelenmiştir.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said. \"The (Hell) Fire is surrounded with all kinds of desires and passions, while Jannah is surrounded with adversities.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/101:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/101:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/101:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001047",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1047",
      "hadith_number": "1047",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن جابر رضي الله عنه قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم : \"مثل الصلوات الخمس كمثل نهر غمر جار على باب أحدكم يغتسل منه كل يوم خمس مرات\".",
      "text_tr": "Câbir’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah : Beş vakit namaz, birinizin kapısı önünde akan ve içinde her gün beş defa yıkandığı suyu bol bir nehir gibidir, buyurmuştur.",
      "text_en": "Jabiru (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"The similitude of the five (obligatory) Salat is like a river running at the door of one of you in which he takes a bath five times a day.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1047:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1047:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1047:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000618",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 618",
      "hadith_number": "618",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعنه أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال:\"بينما رجل يمشى في حلة تعجبه نفسه، مرجل رأسه، يختال في مشيته، إذ خسف الله به، فهو يتجلجل في الأرض إلى يوم القيامة”",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle buyurmuştur: Allah, kibrinden dolayı elbisesini yerde sürükleyen kimseye kıyamet gününde rahmet nazarıyla bakmaz.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"While a man was walking, dressed in clothes admiring himself, his hair combed, walking haughtily when Allah caused the earth to swallow him. Now he will continue to go down in it (as a punishment) until the Day of Resurrection.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/618:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/618:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/618:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000685",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 685",
      "hadith_number": "685",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن عمران بن حصين، رضي الله عنهما، قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: “ الحياء لا يأتى إلا بخير” وفي رواية لمسلم” \"الحياءه خير كله”أوقال: “الحياء كله خير\".",
      "text_tr": "İmrân b. Husayn’dan (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah : Hayâ, sadece hayır getirir, buyurmuştur. (B6117 Buhârî, Edeb, 77; M156 Müslim, İmân, 60) Müslim’in bir diğer rivayetinde: Hayâ, bütünüyle hayırdır, buyrulmuştur.",
      "text_en": "'Imran bin Husain (May Allah be pleased with them) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"Shyness does not bring anything except good.\".In a narration of Muslim: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"All of shyness is good.\"",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/685:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/685:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/685:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000616",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 616",
      "hadith_number": "616",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعنه قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: “ثلاثة لا يكلمهم الله يوم القيامة، ولايزكيهم، ولا ينظر إليهم ، ولهم عذاب أليم: شيخ زان وملك كذاب، وعائل مستكبر”",
      "text_tr": "Hârise b. Vehb’in (ra) Resûlullah’tan şöyle dediğini işittiği nakledilmiştir: Cehennemlikleri size haber vereyim mi? Onlar katı kalpli, büyüklük taslayan, kibirli kimselerdir.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"There are three (types of) people to whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them, nor look at them, and they will have a painful punishment. These are: An aged man who commits Zina (illicit sexual act), a ruler who lies, and a proud poor person.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/616:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/616:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/616:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000123",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 123",
      "hadith_number": "123",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "السابع: عنه عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: \" من غدا إلى المسجد أو راح، أعد الله له في الجنة نزلا كلما غدا أو راح\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Peygamber şöyle buyurmuştur: Bir kimse sabah veya akşam mescide giderse, her gidişinde Allah Teâlâ onun için cennette yer hazırlar.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \"He who goes to the mosque at dawn or dusk (for Salat), Allah prepares a hospitable abode for him in Jannah, every time when he walks to it or comes back from it\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/123:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/123:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/123:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000045",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 45",
      "hadith_number": "45",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي هريرة رضي الله عنه أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: \"ليس الشديد بالصرعة، إنما الشديد الذى يملك نفسه عند الغضب\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle demiştir: Güçlü kimse, insanları güreşte yenen değil, bilakis öfke anında kendisini tutan, iradesine sahip olandır.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"The strong man is not one who is good at wrestling, but the strong man is one who controls himself in a fit of rage.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/45:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/45:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/45:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001567",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1567",
      "hadith_number": "1567",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعنه قال: أتي النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم برجل قد شرب قال: \"اضربوه\" قال أبو هريرة: فمنا الضارب بيده، والضارب بنعله، والضارب بثوبه. فلما انصرف، قال بعض القوم: أخزاك الله، قال: \"لا تقولوا هذا، لا تُعينوا عليه الشيطان\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Zer’in (ra) işittiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle buyurmuştur: “Kimse kimseyi fasıklık veya kâfirlik ile suçlamasın. Zira şayet suçlanan böyle değilse bu sözler kendisine döner.”",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) said: A drunkard was brought to the Prophet (ﷺ). He said, \"Give him a beating.\" Then some beat him with their hands, some with their shoes, and some with (a folded) piece of cloth. When he left, someone said to him: \"May Allah disgrace you!\" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \"Do not help Satan overcome him by uttering such words.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1567:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1567:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1567:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000741",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 741",
      "hadith_number": "741",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "عن أبى هريرة رضى الله عنه قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم : \"إذا دعي أحدكم ، فليجب، فإن كان صائما فليصل، وإن كان مفطراً فليطعم\" .",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah : Biriniz yemeğe davet edildiğinde gitsin. Eğer oruçlu ise davet sahibi için dua etsin. Oruçlu değilse yesin, buyurmuştur.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"When any of you is invited to a meal, he should accept the invitation. If he is observing Saum (fasting), he should supplicate for the betterment of the host and if he is not fasting, he should eat.\" .",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/741:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/741:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/741:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000432",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 432",
      "hadith_number": "432",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي موسى الأشعري، رضي الله عنه، قال: قال رسول الله، صلى الله عليه وسلم: إذا كان يوم القيامة دفع الله إلى كل مسلم يهودياً أونصرانياً فيقول: هذا فكاكك من النار\". وفي رواية عنه عن النبي، صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: \"يجئ يوم القيامة ناس من المسلمين بذنوب أمثال الجبال يغفرها الله لهم \"",
      "text_tr": "Câbir’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle buyurmuştur: Beş vakit namaz, birinizin kapısı önünde akan ve içinde her gün beş kere yıkandığı suyu bol bir nehir gibidir.",
      "text_en": "Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will deliver to every Muslim, a Jew or a Christian and say: 'This is your ransom from Hell-fire.\"'Another narration is: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"There would come people amongst the Muslims on the Day of Resurrection with sins as heavy as a mountain, and Allah would forgive them\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/432:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/432:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/432:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001406",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1406",
      "hadith_number": "1406",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعنه رضي الله عنه قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: \"لا تجعلوا قبري عيدًا وصلوا علي، فإن صلاتكم تبلغني حيث كنتم\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’den nakledildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle buyurmuştur: Kabrimi bayram yerine çevirmeyin. Bana salâvat getirin, nerede olursanız olun, salât ve selâmlarınız bana ulaşır.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"Do not make my grave a place of festivity, and supplicate Allah for me, for your supplication reaches me wherever you are.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1406:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1406:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1406:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000124",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 124",
      "hadith_number": "124",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "الثامن: عنه قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: \" يا نساء المسلمات لا تحقرن جارة لجارتها ولو فرسن شاة\"",
      "text_tr": "Yine Ebû Hüreyre’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle demiştir: Ey Müslüman kadınlar, hiçbir komşu kadın, bir koyun paçası bile olsa, komşusunun ikramını hor görmesin.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: O Muslim women, never belittle any gift you give your neighbour even if it is a hoof of a sheep\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/124:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/124:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/124:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001588",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1588",
      "hadith_number": "1588",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي هريرة رضي الله عنه قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم : \"من خبب زوجة امرئ، أو مملوكه، فليس منا\". \"خَبَب\" بخاء معجمة، ثم باء موحدة مكررة: أي: أفسده وخدعه.",
      "text_tr": "İbn Ömer’den (ra) nakledildiğine göre, Hz. Peygamber , müşteri kızıştırmayı (satın alma niyeti olmadığı hâlde, sırf müşteriyi zarara sokmak için malın değerini arttırmayı) yasakladı.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"He who deceives another's wife or his slave is none of us.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1588:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1588:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1588:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
