    {
      "id": "hadith_000463",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 463",
      "hadith_number": "463",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن جابر، رضي الله عنه أن رسول الله، صلى الله عليه وسلم، مر بالسوق والناس كنفتيه، فمر بجدى أسك ميت، فتناوله، فأخذ بأذنيه، ثم قال: \"أيكم يحب أن يكون هذا له بدرهم؟ \" فقالوا: ما نحب أنه لنا بشئ ومانصنع به؟ ثم قال: “أتحبون أنه لكم؟ قالوا: والله لو كان حياً كان عيباً؛ أنه أسك. فكيف وهو ميت _! فقال: \"فوالله للدنيا أهون على الله من هذا عليكم\" ('قوله: كنفتيه أي: على جانبيه. و الأسك الصغير الأذن.')",
      "text_tr": "Yine Enes’ten (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle buyurmuştur: Üç şey ölenin ardından (mezara kadar) gider: Ailesi, malı ve ameli. Bunlardan ikisi döner, birisi kalır. Dönenler ailesi ve malıdır, kalan ise amelidir.",
      "text_en": "Jabir bin 'Abdullah (May allah be pleased with him) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was passing through the bazaar with his Companions on his both sides, when he saw a dead skinny lamb. He held its ear and said, \"Who of you would like to have it for a dirham\". They replied, \"We do not like to get it for nothing, and what shall we do with it?\". Then he (ﷺ) asked, \"Would you like to have it for nothing?\". They replied, \"Had it been alive, it would have been defective because it is skinny; but when dead it is of no use\". Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"Truly, the world is more contemptible to Allah than this (the dead lamb) is to you\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/463:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/463:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/463:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001066",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1066",
      "hadith_number": "1066",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعنه أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: الملائكة تصلي على أحدكم ما دام في مصلاه الذي صلى فيه ما لم يحدث تقول اللهم اغفر له اللهم ارحمه\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle demiştir: Biriniz, namaz kıldığı yerde abdestini bozmadan oturduğu müddetçe, melekler ona “Allah’ım o kimseyi bağışla, Allah’ım ona merhamet et.” diye dua ederler.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"The angels supplicate in favour of one of you so long as he remains in the place where he has performed Salat (prayer) in a state of Wudu'. They (the angels) say: 'O Allah! Forgive him, O Allah! Have mercy on him.\"'.",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1066:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1066:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1066:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000023",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 23",
      "hadith_number": "23",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن ابن عباس رضي الله عنهما أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: \" لو أن لابن آدم وادياً من ذهب أحب أن يكون له واديان، ولن يملأ فاه إلا التراب، ويتوب الله على من تاب\"",
      "text_tr": "İbn Abbâs ve Enes b. Mâlik’ten (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle demiştir: Âdemoğlunun bir vadi altını olsa ikincisini ister. Onun ağzını topraktan başka bir şey doldurmaz. Allah, tövbe edenin tövbesini kabul eder.",
      "text_en": "Ibn 'Abbas and Anas bin Malik (May Allah be pleased with them) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"If a son of Adam were to own a valley full of gold, he would desire to have two. Nothing can fill his mouth except the earth (of the grave). Allah turns with mercy to him who turns to Him in repentance\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/23:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/23:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/23:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000103",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 103",
      "hadith_number": "103",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "التاسع: عن ابن مسعود رضي الله عنه قال: صليت مع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ليلة، فأطال القيام حتى هممت بأمر سوء! قيل: وما هممت به؟ قال: هممت أن أجلس وأدعه.",
      "text_tr": "İbn Mes’ûd (ra) anlatıyor: Bir gece Peygamber’le birlikte namaz kıldım. Kıyamı o kadar uzattı ki, kötü bir iş yapmayı bile düşündüm, dedi. –Ne yapmayı düşündün, denilince; –Peygamber’i kıyamda bırakıp, oturmayı düşündüm, dedi.",
      "text_en": "Ibn Mas'ud (May Allah be pleased with him) said: One night I joined the Prophet (ﷺ) in his (optional) Salat. He prolonged the standing so much that I thought of doing something evil. He was asked: \"What did you intend to do?\" He replied: \"To sit down and leave him\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/103:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/103:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/103:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000133",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 133",
      "hadith_number": "133",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "السابع عشر: عنه قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم : \" إذا مرض العبد أو سافر كتب له مثل ما كان يعمل مقيماً صحيحاً\"",
      "text_tr": "Yine Ebû Mûsâ’dan (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle buyurmuştur: Bir kimse hastalanır veya (cihad maksadıyla) sefere çıkarsa, sağlıklı ve mukim iken ne tür ameller yapıyor idiyse, ona aynı amellerin sevabı yazılır.",
      "text_en": "Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"When a slave of Allah suffers from illness or sets on a journey, he is credited with the equal of whatever good works he used to do when he was healthy or at home\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/133:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/133:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/133:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000260",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 260",
      "hadith_number": "260",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن سعد بن أبي وقاص رضي الله عنه قال: كنا مع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ستة نفر، فقال المشركون للنبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: اطرد هؤلاء لايجترئون علينا، وكنت أنا وابن مسعود ورجلان لست أسميهما، فوقع في نفس رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم ما شاء الله أن يقع، فحدث نفسه، فأنزل الله تعالى: {ولا تطرد الذين يدعون ربهم بالغداة والعشي يريدون وجهه}",
      "text_tr": "Sehl b. Sa’d’dan (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah : Ben ve yetimin sorumluluğunu üstlenen kimse, cennette şöylece beraber bulunacağız, buyurdu ve şehâdet parmağıyla orta parmağını gösterdi ve iki parmağının arasını açtı.",
      "text_en": "Sa'd bin Abu Waqqas (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: Six of us were with the Prophet (ﷺ) when the infidels said to him: \"Drive these ones away, lest they should begin to venture against us\". The six were, myself, Ibn Mas'ud, a man of the Hudhail tribe, Bilal and two other men whose names I don't know. Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) thought what Allah wished him to think, and Allah revealed: \"And turn not away those who invoke their Rubb, morning and afternoon seeking His Face.\" (6:52).",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/260:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/260:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/260:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001603",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1603",
      "hadith_number": "1603",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن ابن عمر رضي الله عنهما أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: \"إذا كانوا ثلاثة فلا يتناجى اثنان دون الثالث\" ((ورواه أبو دواد وزاد: قال أبو صالح: قلت لابن عمر: فأربعة؟ قال: لا يضرك. ورواه مالك في الموطأ: عن عبد الله بن دينار قال: كنت أنا وابن عمر عند دار خالد بن عقبة التي في السوق، فجاء رجل يريد أن يناجيه، وليس مع ابن عمر أحد غيري، فدعا ابن عمر رجلا آخر حتى كنا أربعة فقال لي وللرجل الثالث الذي دعا: استأخرا شيئًا، فإني سمعت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول: \"لا يتناجى اثنان دون واحد\".",
      "text_tr": "Sahâbî Ebû Hırâş Hadred b. Ebû Hadred el-Eslemî’den (es-Sülemî de denir) (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre o, Peygamber’in şöyle dediğini işitmiştir: “Müslüman kardeşine bir sene küs duran, onun kanını dökmüş gibi günaha girmiştir.”",
      "text_en": "Ibn 'Umar (May Allah be pleased with them) said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"In the presence of three people, two should not hold secret counsel, to the exclusion of the third.\".In Abu Dawud, Abu Salih related: I asked Ibn 'Umar: \"What if there are four people.\" He said, \"There is no harm in that.\"Malik reported in Al-Muwatta that 'Abdullah bin Dinar related: Ibn 'Umar and I were together in Khalid bin 'Uqbah's house which was situated in the market place. A man came to consult Ibn 'Umar. None besides me was present. Ibn 'Umar called another man in and we became four and said to me and the man he had called: Move away a bit because I have heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, \"The two people should not hold secret counsel together excluding the third.\"",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1603:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1603:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1603:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000079",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 79",
      "hadith_number": "79",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "السادس: عن عمر رضي الله عنه قال: سمعت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول : \"لو أنكم تتوكلون على الله حق توكله لرزقكم كما يرزق الطير ، تغدو خماصاً وتروح بطاناً\"",
      "text_tr": "Hz. Ömer’in (ra) Resûlullah’tan şöyle işittiği nakledilmiştir: Eğer Allah’a gereği gibi tevekkül etseydiniz, Allah size kuşlara rızık verdiği gibi rızık verirdi. Kuşlar sabahleyin aç çıkarlar, akşamleyin doymuş olarak dönerler.",
      "text_en": "'Umar (May Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: \"If you all depend on Allah with due reliance, He would certainly give you provision as He gives it to birds who go forth hungry in the morning and return with full belly at dusk\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/79:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/79:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/79:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001363",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1363",
      "hadith_number": "1363",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي هريرة رضي الله عنه قال: قال لي رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم : \"من أعتق رقبة مسلمة أعتق الله بكل عضو منه عضوًا منه من النار حتى فرجه بفرجه\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre o şöyle demiştir: Resûlullah bana şöyle söyledi: Allah Müslüman bir köle azat eden kimsenin, edep yerleri dahil, bütün organlarını, o kölenin organlarına karşılık cehennemden kurtarır.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"He who sets free a Muslim slave, Allah will deliver from the fire of Hell every limb of his body in return for every limb of the slave's body, even his private parts.\".",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1363:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1363:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1363:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_001744",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 1744",
      "hadith_number": "1744",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "عن عائشة رضي الله عنها عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: \"لا يقولن أحدكم خبثت نفسي، ولكن ليقل: لقست نفسي\" قال العلماء معنى خبثت أي غثيت وهو معنى لقست ولكن كره لفظ الخبث",
      "text_tr": "Abdullah b. Amr b. Âs’tan (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle buyurmuştur: Allah, sığırın ağzını evirip çevirdiği gibi, dilini ağzının içinde dolaştıra dolaştıra konuşan (gösteriş için söz sarf eden) kimselere öfkelenir.",
      "text_en": "'Aishah (May Allah be pleased with her) said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \"None of you should say: 'My soul has become evil.' He should say: 'My soul is in bad shape.\"'.",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1744:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1744:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/1744:en",
      "grade": "riyad_as_salihin_selection",
      "source_note": "local approved payload; approved_at=2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
      "topics": [
        "hadis_approved_pool"
      ],
      "status": "approved",
      "durum": "yayina_hazir",
      "priority": 1,
      "book_reference_tr": "",
      "book_reference_en": "",
      "approval": {
        "approved_by": "local_review_tool",
        "approved_at": "2026-06-09T08:35:54+00:00",
        "review_note": "Synced from local approved payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hadith_000927",
      "type": "hadith",
      "collection": "Riyazu's-Salihin",
      "book": "Riyad as-Salihin 927",
      "hadith_number": "927",
      "narrator": "requires verification",
      "text_ar": "وعن أبي هريرة رضي الله عنه أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: يقول الله تعالى: ما لعبدي المؤمن عندي جزاء إذا قبضت صفيه من أهل الدنيا، ثم احتسبه إلا الجنه\"",
      "text_tr": "Ebû Hüreyre’den (ra) rivayet edildiğine göre Resûlullah şöyle demiştir: Allah Teâlâ “Dünyada mümin bir kulumun sevdiğini aldığımda, o bu musibetin ecrini benden sabır ve teslimiyetle beklerse, mükâfatı ancak cennettir.” buyurmuştur.",
      "text_en": "Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Allah, the Exalted, says: 'I have no reward except Jannah for a believing slave of Mine who shows patience and anticipates My reward when I take away his favourite one from the inhabitants of the world.\"'.",
      "source_ar": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/927:ar",
      "source_tr": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/927:tr",
      "source_en": "local_approved:riyazussalihin/927:en",
